00:30:46.510 --> 00:30:49.540
I'm curious how
much frontloading

00:30:49.540 --> 00:30:54.910
that SME adjustment might take
place, like financial growth

00:30:54.910 --> 00:31:01.240
projections or marketing
budgets, things like this?

00:31:01.240 --> 00:31:03.670
How much of that actually
takes place at the beginning?

00:31:03.670 --> 00:31:06.970
And how much of that initial
forecasting is really

00:31:06.970 --> 00:31:10.930
just if the past repeats itself,
here's what would happen.

00:31:10.930 --> 00:31:12.430
And if there's not
a perfect answer,

00:31:12.430 --> 00:31:15.580
because you said there is a
data science team sort of does

00:31:15.580 --> 00:31:19.270
that piece, maybe do you have
a favorite infrastructure

00:31:19.270 --> 00:31:25.130
or framework or resource to
see how these get navigated?

00:31:25.130 --> 00:31:28.580
So the question is about how
much does the finance team make

00:31:28.580 --> 00:31:31.010
their own projections
that they might

00:31:31.010 --> 00:31:33.560
add to our forecast
versus how much is it

00:31:33.560 --> 00:31:37.050
sort of after the fact, once
the forecast is in place?

00:31:37.050 --> 00:31:37.550
Yeah.

00:31:37.550 --> 00:31:39.200
Yeah, exactly.

00:31:39.200 --> 00:31:40.970
I've seen both of
these sort of cases

00:31:40.970 --> 00:31:44.032
happen, where finance
has a 33% growth.

00:31:44.032 --> 00:31:45.240
And that's where we're going.

00:31:45.240 --> 00:31:46.820
So you really
better track on that

00:31:46.820 --> 00:31:49.730
because it's sort of a
self-fulfilling prophecy.

00:31:49.730 --> 00:31:51.860
But I've also seen it where
we start with a vacuum.

00:31:51.860 --> 00:31:54.170
And I'm curious what
your experience has been.

00:31:54.170 --> 00:31:58.410
I'm curious if there's
a best way [INAUDIBLE]??

00:31:58.410 --> 00:31:58.910
Gotcha.

00:31:58.910 --> 00:31:59.410
Yeah.

00:31:59.410 --> 00:32:01.340
So I think our
approach has typically

00:32:01.340 --> 00:32:04.400
been to divide the
forecast into segments.

00:32:04.400 --> 00:32:07.118
So there are-- I
alluded to this earlier.

00:32:07.118 --> 00:32:09.410
There are places where the
statistical models do really

00:32:09.410 --> 00:32:09.990
well.

00:32:09.990 --> 00:32:11.870
We have enough history.

00:32:11.870 --> 00:32:16.250
There's not a lot of external
factors that influence that.

00:32:16.250 --> 00:32:18.620
It's sort of a
continuous time series

00:32:18.620 --> 00:32:20.730
that we can forecast
pretty well.

00:32:20.730 --> 00:32:25.760
And so we sort of explain that
to the finance and strategy

00:32:25.760 --> 00:32:29.420
team and work with them and
show them the statistics on it.

00:32:29.420 --> 00:32:32.570
And then we find that there
are other places where

00:32:32.570 --> 00:32:35.540
that kind of financial
modeling is very fruitful

00:32:35.540 --> 00:32:39.890
and is very helpful to adjusting
the forecast, where there are

00:32:39.890 --> 00:32:42.620
things that the statistical
model will do less well

00:32:42.620 --> 00:32:45.890
or might not know
about or really could

00:32:45.890 --> 00:32:46.940
use some adjustment.

00:32:46.940 --> 00:32:51.890
And that's how, in
those places, we really

00:32:51.890 --> 00:32:53.720
open it up and
encourage adjustments.

00:32:53.720 --> 00:32:56.562
I actually think we could have
even more process control.

00:32:56.562 --> 00:32:58.520
We were just talking
about controls around this

00:32:58.520 --> 00:33:01.580
and around how we do
the adjustment process.

00:33:01.580 --> 00:33:05.873
That's something I'd like
us to continue to work on.

00:33:05.873 --> 00:33:07.290
But that's generally
how it works.

00:33:07.290 --> 00:33:09.373
So the finance team does
do some modeling and does

00:33:09.373 --> 00:33:12.210
have their sort of
priors, if you will,

00:33:12.210 --> 00:33:15.080
that they're adjusting
the forecast by.

00:33:15.080 --> 00:33:17.390
But we work together
to make sure

00:33:17.390 --> 00:33:19.908
that they are spending their
effort in the right ways when

00:33:19.908 --> 00:33:20.450
they do this.

00:33:25.230 --> 00:33:26.260
Thank you.

00:33:26.260 --> 00:33:28.950
Yu, I'm sorry I didn't notice
